# Flutter Typography & Spacing Rules

## Typography

Use `AppTypography.*` helpers for all semantic text styles. Do NOT create standalone `TextStyle` with explicit `fontFamily` or `fontSize` outside of `app_typography.dart` and `main.dart`.

```dart
import '../utils/app_typography.dart';

AppTypography.heading1(context)   // 24sp bold     — screen titles
AppTypography.heading2(context)   // 20sp semi-bold — section titles
AppTypography.sectionTitle(context) // alias for heading2
AppTypography.heading3(context)   // 18sp semi-bold — card titles
AppTypography.body(context)       // 16sp regular  — main content
AppTypography.bodySmall(context)  // 14sp regular  — secondary content
AppTypography.caption(context)    // 12sp regular  — hints, metadata
AppTypography.secondary(context)  // 14sp onSurfaceVariant
AppTypography.button(context)     // 16sp medium   — button labels
AppTypography.error(context)      // 14sp error colour
```

For standard Material roles you can also use:
```dart
Theme.of(context).textTheme.bodyLarge
Theme.of(context).textTheme.labelLarge
// etc.
```

## What NOT to do

```dart
// ❌ Explicit fontFamily
TextStyle(fontSize: 16, fontFamily: 'Inter')

// ❌ Explicit fontFamily with GoogleFonts (already global)
GoogleFonts.inter(fontSize: 16)

// ❌ Hardcoded fontSize in a widget build()
Text('Hello', style: TextStyle(fontSize: 18, fontWeight: FontWeight.w600))
```

## Spacing

Use `AppSpacing` constants — never hardcode pixel values.

```dart
import '../utils/app_spacing.dart';

AppSpacing.xs    // 4.0   — tight gaps, icon padding
AppSpacing.sm    // 8.0   — standard gap
AppSpacing.md    // 16.0  — content padding
AppSpacing.lg    // 24.0  — section gap
AppSpacing.xl    // 32.0  — large section gap
AppSpacing.xxl   // 48.0  — hero spacing

// Border radii
AppSpacing.radiusBadge   // 6.0
AppSpacing.radiusChip    // 8.0
AppSpacing.radiusInput   // 12.0
AppSpacing.radiusDialog  // 20.0
AppSpacing.radiusCard    // 24.0
```

### Standard card padding
```dart
padding: const EdgeInsets.all(AppSpacing.md)
```

### Standard list item padding
```dart
padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(
  horizontal: AppSpacing.md,
  vertical: AppSpacing.sm,
)
```

## Touch Targets

Keep interactive elements at minimum **48×48** logical pixels.
